    {
      "type": "exercise",
      "id": "review-grammar-vocabulary-4",
      "title": "Read the article. Circle a, b, or c.",
      "layout": "continuous-gaps",
      "introTitle": "How to take good photos of children",
      "hideAnswersOnError": true,
      "paragraphs": [
        [
          "In photography, one of the hardest shots to take is a ",
          {
            "type": "gap",
            "id": "1",
            "input": "select",
            "options": [
              "flash",
              "landscape",
              "close-up"
            ],
            "answer": "close-up"
          },
          " of a child. If you’re taking photos ",
          {
            "type": "gap",
            "id": "2",
            "input": "select",
            "options": [
              "inside",
              "into",
              "on"
            ],
            "answer": "inside"
          },
          " a room, you’ll need a lot of light. Position the child near a window, but make sure the sun isn’t shining ",
          {
            "type": "gap",
            "id": "3",
            "input": "select",
            "options": [
              "across",
              "past",
              "through"
            ],
            "answer": "through"
          },
          " the window into the room. However, the ",
          {
            "type": "gap",
            "id": "4",
            "input": "select",
            "options": [
              "best",
              "better",
              "good"
            ],
            "answer": "best"
          },
          " place to photograph children is outside. Wait until late afternoon or early evening when the sun is low in the sky. The most difficult children to capture are ",
          {
            "type": "gap",
            "id": "5",
            "input": "select",
            "options": [
              "babies",
              "teenagers",
              "toddlers"
            ],
            "answer": "toddlers"
          },
          " – they’re never still as they’ve just learned to walk. The other problem is that children are usually ",
          {
            "type": "gap",
            "id": "6",
            "input": "select",
            "options": [
              "a bit",
              "much",
              "very"
            ],
            "answer": "much"
          },
          " more interested in playing than in posing for a photo. You have to be ",
          {
            "type": "gap",
            "id": "7",
            "input": "select",
            "options": [
              "considerate",
              "creative",
              "thoughtless"
            ],
            "answer": "creative"
          },
          " about getting their attention. You can use a noisy toy to get them to look ",
          {
            "type": "gap",
            "id": "8",
            "input": "select",
            "options": [
              "after",
              "towards",
              "for"
            ],
            "answer": "towards"
          },
          " the camera, but don’t show it ",
          {
            "type": "gap",
            "id": "9",
            "input": "select",
            "options": [
              "at them",
              "for them",
              "to them"
            ],
            "answer": "to them"
          },
          " beforehand, or it won’t be a surprise. Some ",
          {
            "type": "gap",
            "id": "10",
            "input": "select",
            "options": [
              "photographers",
              "photography",
              "photographs"
            ],
            "answer": "photographers"
          },
          " ask a friend to help distract the child while they try to get a picture. It isn’t unusual to see an adult running round a room while another is taking photos of a child watching them."
        ]
      ]
    }
